Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: clk: sunxi-ng: h616: Let the S/PDIF clock set the audio PLL rate

sun4i-spdif asks for 22.5792 or 24.576 MHz on the OWA module clock (H616
user manual v1.0, 8.3: Fs = PLL_AUDIO / ((TX_RATIO + 1) * 128)). The
spdif clock has no CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, so the rate can only be met if the
codec or the audio hub has already retuned pll-audio to the right
family. Otherwise the power-of-two divider rounds down and the request
"succeeds" at a wrong rate (about 12.3 MHz from the reset PLL value,
i.e. 48 kHz content played at about 24 kHz). Propagate the rate to the
PLL, as the codec clocks already do.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@
 		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS("spdif",
 						      audio_parents,
 						      &ccu_div_ops,
-						      0),
+						      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT),
 	},
 };
 
